<h1>Tools</h1>
<p class="wip-badge">Work in progress</p>
<p>Planned interactive tools, beyond the generated reference pages this wiki already has:</p>

<h2>Schematic viewer/uploader</h2>
<p class="wip-badge">Work in progress</p>
<p>
  Upload a <code>.json</code> schematic file and view it rendered in the browser, and (longer
  term) browse this wiki's own structure schematics the same way instead of just dimensions/block
  counts. Likely needs adapting code from
  <a href="https://github.com/jgwoolley/vintage-story-schematic-preview">jgwoolley/vintage-story-schematic-preview</a>.
</p>

<h2>Painting/tapestry-in-ruins lookup</h2>
<p class="wip-badge">Work in progress</p>
<p>
  Right now, each <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}paintings/">painting</a>/
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}tapestries/">tapestry</a> page shows which
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}structures/">structures</a> it's found in, built from a
  flat pass over every schematic's block-code dictionary. A proper lookup still needs to be
  evaluated against <code>worldgen/storystructures.json</code> and <code>worldgen/structures.json</code>
  directly, to confirm which specific ruin/story-structure variants actually place a given
  painting or tapestry (rather than just "some schematic somewhere contains this block code").
</p>
